# jwt-demo.http
# Click the green arrow next to a request to run it.
# If you changed PORT in .env, change it here too.
@host = http://localhost:3001

# After you run request 2, paste the accessToken here (no quotes)
@token = paste_your_token_here

### 1. Public GET /posts (version 1 returns all 3 posts)
GET {{host}}/posts

### 2. Log in as Jake. Copy the accessToken from the response into @token above.
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Jake"
}

### 3. Login with no userName (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3b. Log in as someone we don't know (expect 401)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Thelma"
}

### 4. PART 8 (version 2): GET /posts with Jake's token (expect only Jake's post)
GET {{host}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. GET /posts with no token (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/posts

### 6. GET /posts with an edited token (expect 401)
# Adding "x" to the end changes the signature, so verify fails
GET {{host}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### 7. Log in as GrandPa. Paste this new accessToken into @token above.
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "GrandPa"
}

### 8. Rerun GET /posts with GrandPa's token (expect only GrandPa's post)
GET {{host}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}